āṅkadevacarita. in 18 sarga.\nPt.. (1) Bomb. Skt. "},{"t":"cite","s":"Ser. 14","q":"Ser"},{"t":"txt","s":". (2) Princess of Wales Sar. Bha. "},{"t":"cite","s":"Texts. 82","q":"Texts"},{"t":"txt","s":".\nThe following works are ascribed to him:\n--a Rāmacarita or Rāmastuti.\n--a. Alaṅkāraśāstra.\nSee Rice, JRAS. NS. XV. p. 305."}]}]}],"bilhaRa(kavi)":[{"id":"bilhaRa(kavi)","headword":"बिल्हण(कवि)","headword_slp1":"bilhaRa(kavi)","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Bilhaṇa(kavi)\nins. poet. favourite an. trusted Prime minister of King Vindhyavarmadeva (1160-1180) of Dhara of Paramāras of Malwa; also a resident of Dhara; praises Āśādhara; composed the inscription of Maṇḍu (a hymn to God Viṣṇu) of Vindhyavarmadeva.\nC.. biracitamiha biSNodami vAkyaprasUnaizcaraNasatatapUjA bAkkRtA bilhaNena … viMdhyavarmanRpateH prasAdabhUH sAMghivigrahikabilhaNakaviH etc. ed. by K. K. Lele, Dhar, ABORI. "},{"t":"cite","s":"XI. 49","q":""},{"t":"txt","s":"ff. [Page008-a."}]},{"n":2,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Bilhaṇa(kavi)\n--Trirūpakośa. lex.\nSee NCC. VIII. p. 259a."}]},{"n":3,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Bilhaṇa(kavi)\n--"},{"t":"cite","s":"Bilhaṇastava. 39","q":"Bilhaṇastava"},{"t":"txt","s":" v..\nSee below."}]}]}],"bilhaRakavya":[{"id":"bilhaRakAvya","headword":"बिल्हणकाव्य","headword_slp1":"bilhaRakAvya","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Bilhaṇakāvya\nBaroda "},{"t":"cite","s":"II. 13460","q":""},{"t":"txt","s":" (c). BISM. (Pt.. Cat.) 53/161. Deo 166. "},{"t":"cite","s":"IM. 375","q":""},{"t":"txt","s":" (inc.).\nC.. Bilhaṇacarita below."}]}]}],"bilhaRacarita":[{"id":"bilhaRacarita","headword":"बिल्हणचरित","headword_slp1":"bilhaRacarita","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Bilhaṇacarita\nincorporating the Caurapañcāśikā traditionally ascribed to Bilhaṇa; said to have been composed to record a secret intrigue with a princess Candralekhā, daughter of Vīrasim3ha of Mahilapattana according to Kashmir version an. Yāminīpūrṇatilakā, daughter of Madanābhirāma of Pāñc